# Layout

The create-next-app tree currently uses root `app/`. New fullstack code should grow toward:

```
src/
  app/                 # routes; _components/ (+ optional _data.ts) colocated per route
  server/
    actions/           # Server Actions by domain
    db/client.ts
    db/schema.ts
    services/          # framework-agnostic logic
    auth.ts
  lib/
    mock-data/          # static/demo/placeholder content, typed constants — see ui-separation.mdc
    schemas/            # Zod schemas
    constants.ts
    utils.ts
  components/          # shared UI (used by 2+ routes)
  types/
```

Prefer native Next.js (Server Actions, RSC, `revalidatePath`/`revalidateTag`) over new libraries unless native cannot do the job.

Do **not** follow `docs/architecture.md`'s Route Handler + TanStack Query request/data-fetching pattern (`src/services/`, `src/hooks/api/`, fetch-based mutations) — Server Actions replace that here. Its general layering principle (small, single-purpose files; nothing duplicated across layers) still applies and is spelled out for UI code in `ui-separation.mdc`.
